{"requirements":[{"id":"daily-rotation","requirement":"Rotate /var/log/inventory/app.log daily.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The installed policy specifies daily rotation; logrotate successfully parsed it as rotating after one day, and the enabled, active systemd timer has OnCalendar=daily and Persistent=true. A forced rotation also demonstrated that the policy operates successfully.","evidence_ids":["cmd-52f6c9fe782048c9","cmd-892f09170bcd4e9b","cmd-6c64a43492574f8f","cmd-9f72df5f7f6a4048","cmd-b5a579a4e42948cf"]},{"id":"retention-compression","requirement":"Keep seven compressed rotations of /var/log/inventory/app.log.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The policy specifies rotate 7 and compress; parser output confirms the seven-rotation setting, and the forced rotation produced a valid gzip archive that remained intact after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-52f6c9fe782048c9","cmd-892f09170bcd4e9b","cmd-6c64a43492574f8f","cmd-167924818ff941b6","cmd-b5a579a4e42948cf"]},{"id":"continued-writing","requirement":"Allow the application to continue writing after rotation.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A file descriptor was held open across a forced rotation using copytruncate. The live log retained the same inode, accepted a post-rotation write through that descriptor, and preserved the pre-rotation marker in the compressed archive. Writability was also confirmed after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-6c64a43492574f8f","cmd-b5a579a4e42948cf"]}],"confidence":0.96,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1.0,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Installing the logrotate policy was required; the forced rotation and marker writes were bounded behavioral evidence; and the reboot scheduling was required by the provider-wide restart protocol. No failed services, new network exposure, package damage, or unrelated temporary residue was observed afterward. The restart protocol is complete: healthy pre-restart policy/timer/data state and boot identity, restart acknowledgement, a changed post-restart boot identity independently confirmed by lifecycle capture, and recovered timer, policy, archives, data, and writability.","evidence_ids":["cmd-52f6c9fe782048c9","cmd-6c64a43492574f8f","cmd-167924818ff941b6","cmd-b82dea92517b4423","cmd-18ba06422ace4aca","cmd-b5a579a4e42948cf","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes are satisfied. The daily seven-generation compressed logrotate policy was installed and parsed successfully, rotation behavior and continued writes were directly exercised, and the configuration and data recovered across a fully evidenced node restart. Operational hygiene is clean.","limitations":["The evidence directly demonstrates one compressed rotation, but does not exercise accumulation and pruning at the seven-archive boundary.","Daily scheduling is established by the active systemd timer and parsed policy; no naturally elapsed daily timer invocation was observed during the short evidence window."]}
